{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/defaultPosition(_:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/defaultposition(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that specifies where to place a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completely obscuring existing windows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same unit point.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing"},{"text":" in the above example — but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window in the y-dimension:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in macOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"namely:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Window","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Settings","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last occupied.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE15defaultPositionyQrAA9UnitPointVF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11OpenSwiftUI11WindowGroupV","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"defaultPosition(_:)","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Sets a default position for a window.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","title":"OpenSwiftUI","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","role":"collection"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowGroup":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowGroup"}],"type":"topic","title":"WindowGroup","abstract":[{"text":"A scene that presents a group of identically structured windows.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowGroup"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup","role":"symbol"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Scene":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scene"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scene","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A part of an app’s user interface with a life cycle managed by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scene"}],"title":"Scene","kind":"symbol"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowGroup/defaultPosition(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/defaultPosition(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets a default position for a window."}],"title":"defaultPosition(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/defaultposition(_:)"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/UnitPoint":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/unitpoint","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"topic","title":"UnitPoint","abstract":[{"text":"A normalized 2D point in a view’s coordinate space.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/UnitPoint/bottomTrailing":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"bottomTrailing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UnitPoint"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A point that’s in the bottom, trailing corner of a view."}],"title":"bottomTrailing","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/unitpoint\/bottomtrailing","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}